# REQ-011: Patient Matching

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** High
**Risk:** Critical (wrong patient match is a patient safety risk)
**Depends On:** REQ-001 (Unified Inbound Document Inbox), REQ-002 (Electronic Inbound Ingestion), REQ-009 (Audit Trail)

---

## User Story

As a practice administrator,
I need inbound documents to be automatically matched to the correct patient,
So that documents are filed against the right patient record without requiring manual lookup for every document.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] The system automatically attempts to match every inbound document to a patient in the EMIS Web patient register. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] NHSmail attachments are ingested as document source records and enter the Document Manager matching flow. The NHSmail service does not provide an authoritative patient match for Document Manager. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The primary matching signal is the NHS Number extracted from the document. Where the NHS Number passes Modulus 11 validation and uniquely matches a patient in the EMIS Web register, the match is confirmed automatically — no user confirmation step is required. The matched document is routed to the Filing Queue (if filing metadata requires completion) or directly to the Tasking Queue (if metadata is fully embedded and routing rules apply). *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Where the matching confidence is insufficient for automatic confirmation (no valid NHS Number extractable, the NHS Number does not match a unique patient, or multiple candidate patients are found), the document is routed to the Unmatched tab for manual review. The user selects the correct patient from EMIS Web search results; the selected record’s EMIS Web patient identifier is used to confirm the match. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The user can manually search for a different patient and override the auto-suggested match at any point before the document is routed. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Where no match can be determined, the document is placed in an unmatched queue for manual review — it is never silently discarded or auto-filed without a match. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] All auto-matches, manual match resolutions, and overrides are audited. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] A user can re-open the patient matching workflow from the Filing, Coding, or Task Queue at any point to undo, modify, or replace a previously confirmed patient match. This action is audited. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] When a patient match is changed after a document has been filed, the system warns the user that the change will update the document’s attribution in the patient record and requires explicit confirmation before proceeding. *(Must Have — CLIN-007)*

