## Parking Lot

- � **Patient match confidence threshold — defined (2026-05-26)**

  High-confidence path: NHS Number (Modulus 11 validated) + unique patient register match → auto-match, no user confirmation required. All other cases → Unmatched tab for manual review. V1e clinical safety review to confirm thresholds are clinically appropriate.

- 🔴 **Provisional clinician visibility on auto-match — blocked pending CSO sign-off**

  Proposal to allow provisional document visibility before match confirmation — on the basis that speed of clinician access is a priority. Blocked pending formal clinical safety analysis and explicit Clinical Safety Officer sign-off. **Do not implement without CSO sign-off.** (HAZ-DOC-035 — Critical risk: wrong-patient document exposure.)

- ⚪ **Fuzzy / partial patient matching with confidence-based recommendations (future phase)**

  The current binary model (NHS Number match → Matched; otherwise → Unmatched queue) is the V1 baseline. A future phase should explore automated partial matching using demographic signals — for example, name and address similarity — to surface a ranked list of candidate patient records with a confidence recommendation, rather than routing straight to the unmatched queue.

  **What this would look like:**
  - Where no NHS Number is present or valid, the matching engine runs a partial match against name, date of birth, and/or address fields extracted from the document
  - One or more candidate patients are surfaced to the user with a confidence recommendation (e.g. "Strong match", "Possible match", "Weak match")
  - The user selects from the candidates or discards them and searches manually
  - Explicit user confirmation is still required before any match is committed

  **Why parked:**
  - The matching algorithm, confidence signal definitions, and threshold values are not yet specified
  - Partial matching on demographic data introduces additional patient safety risk (HAZ-DOC-032) that requires formal clinical safety analysis before implementation
  - The UX for candidate presentation requires usability research

  **When to revisit:** Once the binary matching model is validated in production, gather data on the volume and resolution rate of unmatched documents to size the value of partial matching. Algorithm specification, confidence threshold definition, and clinical safety analysis (V1e) must precede any implementation decision.

