## Patient Match — Two-Path Model (Auto-match / Manual Review)

> Patient matching uses a two-path model:
>
> **High-confidence path (auto-match):** Where the NHS Number passes Modulus 11 validation and uniquely matches a patient in the EMIS Web register, the match is confirmed automatically without requiring user action. Auto-matched documents are routed to the Filing Queue (if filing metadata requires completion) or directly to the Tasking Queue (if metadata is fully embedded and routing rules apply). Auto-matches are audited with `match_source: auto_nhsnumber`.
>
> **Manual review path (Unmatched tab):** Where no valid NHS Number can be extracted, the extracted NHS Number does not match any patient, or multiple candidate patients are found, the document is routed to the Unmatched tab. The user must manually search for and select the correct patient before the document proceeds. Manual matches are audited with `match_source: manual`.
>
> In all cases, a confirmed patient match can be undone or changed from any queue tab (Filing, Coding, Tasks) subject to explicit re-confirmation and audit.

