## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-001:** NHS Number Validation — NHS Number used for matching must pass Modulus 11 validation before being used as a matching signal
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — all match suggestions, acceptances, and overrides audited
- **CLIN-006:** Patient Identifier Validation — patient identifiers used in matching are GUIDs/ERNs; database PKs never exposed
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — matched patient name displayed visibly in queue list row; user confirmation required before filing
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — matching failures (no match found, multiple candidates) must never result in silent auto-filing; always route to manual review

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-032:** Document filed against wrong patient — clinical decisions made using another patient's document; potential for serious harm
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Low–Medium
  - **Risk Level:** Critical

- **HAZ-DOC-033:** Unmatched document silently lost — no patient match found and document discarded without user awareness
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-034:** Invalid NHS Number used as matching signal — malformed number matches incorrectly or bypasses validation
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-035:** Provisional visibility exposes document to wrong clinician before match is confirmed
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Medium (if provisional visibility implemented without safeguards)
  - **Risk Level:** Critical — **implementation blocked pending CSO sign-off**

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-031:** User confirmation required before any document is filed against a patient match; auto-filing without confirmation not permitted
  - **Type:** Business Logic + UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-032:** Unmatched documents routed to dedicated unmatched queue; never silently discarded
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-033:** NHS Number validated via Modulus 11 before use as matching signal; invalid numbers not used for matching
  - **Type:** Validation
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-034:** Matched patient name displayed in the queue document list row and at the match confirmation step; unmatched documents visually distinguished from matched documents
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Partial (user must still review and confirm)

