## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance

### Product KPIs
- Auto-match success rate (documents successfully auto-matched vs. total inbound)
- Match acceptance rate (user accepts suggested match vs. overrides)
- Override rate (proxy for match quality; high override rate indicates matching needs improvement)
- Unmatched queue size / clearance rate
- Match processing latency (document received → match suggestion available)

### Observable Events (OTEL Instrumentation)
- `documents.matching.initiated` — auto-match process started for document
- `documents.matching.matched` — match suggestion produced
- `documents.matching.unmatched` — no match found; document routed to unmatched queue
- `documents.matching.accepted` — user accepts suggested match
- `documents.matching.overridden` — user overrides suggested match; new patient ERN recorded
- `documents.matching.filed` — document successfully filed against confirmed patient

### Performance SLOs
- Match suggestion latency: p95 < 5 seconds from document ingestion to match suggestion available
- Auto-match success rate: target ≥ 85% of inbound documents auto-matched (baseline TBC from pilot data)

### Alerting Conditions

| Condition | Threshold | Severity | Channel |
|---|---|---|---|
| Match suggestion latency breach | p95 > 5 seconds sustained for 5 min | HIGH | Ops alert |
| Auto-match success rate drop | < 85% over rolling 1-hour window | HIGH | Ops alert |
| Unmatched queue depth spike | > 2× baseline unmatched queue depth | MEDIUM | Ops alert |
| NHS Number validation failure spike | > 5% of documents with extracted NHS Numbers failing Modulus 11 | MEDIUM | Ops alert |

